"""I taught myself to fix bikes off YouTube videos, mostly because I couldn't afford to keep paying the shop downtown. The first derailleur I adjusted, I actually made worse, some cable tension thing I didn't understand yet, and had to bring it in anyway, a little embarrassed. The guy at the shop showed me what I'd done wrong instead of just fixing it silently, which I appreciated more than he probably knows. I've fixed maybe a dozen bikes since then for neighbors, usually for free, sometimes for pizza. I'm not sure I'm good enough to do it professionally. But I like the specific kind of quiet that happens when I'm working on something with my hands and nothing else.""",

